# E234 - Conan dependency-closure refresh requires a new binary identity
id:                     E234
trigger_tool:           conan|cmake|ld
phase:                  dependency-resolution|configuration|linking
error_signature:        missing.*binary.*after.*override|SDL2Config\.cmake|cannot find -lSDL2
severity:               2
category:               conan|dependency-closure|cmake|cross-compilation
match_keywords:         exact version conflict, override, package ID, recipe suffix, SDL2Config.cmake, OHOS toolchain, target sysroot
title:                  Exact dependency override requires a new package identity and target-toolchain binding
root_cause:             A Conan package ID includes settings, options, and the resolved dependency graph. Replacing an exact transitive provider with a newer ABI-compatible provider changes the downstream binary closure even when source files are unchanged. A Windows-hosted CMake invocation also keeps host linker rules unless the official target toolchain establishes the OHOS system, target triple, sysroot, lld, and archiver before the compiler probe. Native CMake config filenames are case-sensitive and cannot be inferred from generated Conan targets.
affected_scope:         Windows-hosted Conan cross builds for CMake libraries whose published binary depends on an older exact provider, especially when the target SDK is OpenHarmony and the downstream consumer uses an exported CMake target.
verification_cmd:       conan graph info <recipe> --build=never; conan create <recipe> -pr:h=<ohos-profile> -pr:b=<windows-profile>; cmake --build <test-package> -- -j2
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           versioned-closure-and-official-target-toolchain
rec_description:        Use the next adaptation version rather than replacing a released recipe revision. Declare one exact provider version and preserve transitive headers/libs. Before CMake configure, verify the provider's real native Config.cmake filename and bind its directory. In the host profile load the SDK's official OHOS toolchain, which sets CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME, target triple, sysroot, lld, and llvm-ar. Re-resolve the full graph, build the new package, and compile the independent consumer set against the resulting package identity.
rec_command:            self.requires("sdl2/2.32.10"); tools.cmake.cmaketoolchain:user_toolchain=["<sdk>/native/build/cmake/ohos.toolchain.cmake"]; test -f "<package>/lib/cmake/SDL2/SDL2Config.cmake"
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               recipe-and-profile
forbid_1_pattern:       keep.*same.*version.*new.*dependency|--build=missing.*as.*publication
forbid_1_reason:        The new dependency graph produces a different package ID and a local build does not make that binary available from the release remote.
forbid_1_consequence:   Downstream CI either selects the incompatible old binary or fails at install; local fallback evidence is misreported as publication.
forbid_2_pattern:       CMAKE_C_COMPILER_TARGET.*without.*CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME|assume.*sdl2-config\.cmake
forbid_2_reason:        Target flags alone do not change host CMake link rules, and a lowercase config filename is not interchangeable with the published SDL2Config.cmake.
forbid_2_consequence:   Compiler probes use host linker libraries or generation fails before source compilation.
principles:             P010,P013,P014
causes:                 []
caused_by:              []
similar_to:             E207,E213
conflicts_with:         []
prerequisite_of:        []
